---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, PUBLISHER } from '../consts';
const desc = 'Who runs App-Tipps.com, how we work, how we are funded, and how to reach the editorial team.';
---
<Base title="About Us" description={desc} schema={{
  '@type': 'AboutPage', '@id': `${SITE.url}/about/#about`,
  mainEntity: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#organization` },
}}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose" style="padding:34px 0 10px">
      <h1>About App-Tipps.com</h1>
      <p class="standfirst" style="font-size:19px;color:var(--ink-soft)">
        App-Tipps.com is an independent publication about mobile apps and games. We have been
        publishing since 2020 and have produced more than 300 articles for readers on iOS and Android.
      </p>

      <h2>What we publish</h2>
      <p>
        We cover four things: reviews of apps and games, guides that help you get further in a game or
        get more out of an app, comparisons between competing products, and news about the mobile
        industry. Everything is written for people choosing what to install and what to spend time on.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not publish sponsored articles disguised as editorial, we do not accept payment for a
        review score, and we do not republish other publications' work. Our full standards, including
        how our review scores are calculated and how we handle corrections, are set out in our
        <a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        App-Tipps.com is published by {PUBLISHER.legalName}, a company registered in England and Wales.
        Editorial responsibility for everything on this site rests with the publisher.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our writers publish under consistent pen names rather than their legal names. They are real
        people on our editorial team, and a byline is used consistently by the same writer. The pen
        names are an editorial convention, not a way of avoiding accountability: the publisher named
        here is answerable for every article on this site. If you need to verify the authorship of a
        specific article for a professional reason, write to us and we will deal with it directly.
      </p>

      <h2>How we are funded</h2>
      <p>
        This site is free to read and is funded by advertising and by affiliate links. When an article
        contains affiliate links, a notice appears at the top of that article. If you buy or sign up
        through one, we may earn a commission at no additional cost to you.
      </p>
      <p>
        Commercial relationships never determine our verdicts. An advertiser cannot buy a better score,
        and we will criticise a product we earn commission on if it deserves criticism.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        If we get something wrong, we want to fix it. Email <a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.editorialEmail}`}>{PUBLISHER.editorialEmail}</a> with
        the article URL and what is inaccurate. Substantive corrections are noted on the article itself.
      </p>

      <h2>Company details</h2>
      <dl>
        <dt>Publisher</dt><dd>{PUBLISHER.legalName}</dd>
        <dt>Registered in</dt><dd>England and Wales</dd>
        <dt>Company number</dt><dd>{PUBLISHER.companyNumber}</dd>
        <dt>VAT number</dt><dd>{PUBLISHER.vatNumber}</dd>
        <dt>Registered office</dt>
        <dd>{PUBLISHER.address.street}, {PUBLISHER.address.city} {PUBLISHER.address.postcode}, {PUBLISHER.address.country}</dd>
        <dt>Editorial contact</dt><dd><a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.editorialEmail}`}>{PUBLISHER.editorialEmail}</a></dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
